  "promptSpec": {
    "id": "d-horse",
    "generator": "OpenAI imagegen built-in",
    "prompt": "Use case: stylized-concept. Production game sprites: original fan-made D-Horse from Metal Gear Solid V The Phantom Pain, based on in-game Equipment D-Horse model. Faithful mature white/light cream Andalusian horse, pale gray-taupe mane and long tail, dark gray muzzle, simple worn brown military saddle and rectangular brown saddle blanket, dark leather bridle and reins, metal stirrups. No rider, no eyepatch, no armor, no ceremonial tassels, no fantasy features. Detailed crisp pixel art in side orthographic profile facing RIGHT throughout. EXACT 4 columns ×4 rows=16 separately drawn full-body poses on flat pure #FF00FF magenta background, thin pure cyan grid guides at each boundary. Maintain ONE identical body scale throughout. Entire horse including all extended legs, mane and tail must fit in CENTRAL SIXTY PERCENT of EACH square cell with a full 20% width empty magenta margin on left and right. Common baseline 80% cell height. Row1 four distinct quiet idle breathing/ear/head phases. Row2 four genuine alternating walking gait phases, anatomically correct four legs. Row3 interaction sequence: lower head gently, nod, turn ears, return head upright. Row4 alert reaction: slight rear-brace, front hooves stepping, tense neck, settle. Never high rear or long jump. No text, no UI, no scenery, no drop shadow, no light gray floor, no ground strokes. Horse and tack entire and consistent in every cell; absolutely no clipping.",
    "generatedFile": "exec-105b7cff-28d2-4f92-bb24-8c31eb5ec2d3.png",
    "referenceUrls": [
      "https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-horse-in-pc-gaming/",
      "https://eu-support.konami.com/hc/en-gb/articles/9668972984727-The-Phantom-Pain-Tactical-Buddies"
    ],
    "review": "Generated image visually reviewed against online game imagery for recognizable silhouette, equipment and complete cell geometry. Original pixel adaptation, no certified 1:1 claim."
  },
